Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4.3 Example: L = 6", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"75a9db82-56f6-954e-9f8a-a784f0451f87"],

Cell["\<\
Parameters: J = 1, q = Pi/3 (pitch 6 sites, so the helix makes 5/6 of a turn \
across the chain), Delta = cos q = 1/2 (easy plane), theta = 1.1 (tilted out \
of the plane, so the state spans all S^z sectors with non-trivial weights), \
phi0 = 0, bL = 0.2, bR = -0.1 (generic, non-symmetric longitudinal parts), w \
= 0.5. The total time covers two full periods 2 Pi / w.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"765d73ac-2876-7e43-840a-72537d7a9fb9"],

